<title>JAPAN: MOF hopes to start deregulation once steps ready.</title>
<headline>MOF hopes to start deregulation once steps ready.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Vice Minister of Finance Tadashi Ogawa told a news conference on Thursday that his ministry hopes to implement financial deregulation steps as soon as they are ready.  </p>
<p>Asked about the ruling Liberal Democratic Party's proposal to scrap the tax on securities transactions from fiscal 1998/99, Ogawa said:</p>
<p>&quot;We hope to implement the contents of the deregulation measures as soon as they are ready.&quot;</p>
</text>
